    "done_when": "reckon/cli.py registers a `hooks` group with an `install` command, --scope user and --write, wrapping install_hook_settings from reckon/hooks/install.py without reimplementing it. By default the command prints the fragment and opens no file. With --write it merges into the user-scope settings file, and it refuses, exiting non-zero with the installer's message, when an entry with the same command is already present. A new tests/test_hooks_install_cli.py drives the command through the click test runner three ways: the dry run, which prints the fragment and leaves the target byte-identical; a write into a temporary settings file; and the duplicate refusal. Every test points the settings path at a temporary directory, and asserts afterwards that the real ~/.claude/settings.json is byte-identical to before the test. skills/reckon-build/references/orchestrator-harness/claude-code.md replaces its interim python -c install instructions with the command, and names no host path. One base log and one head log over tests/test_hooks_install_cli.py tests/test_hook_installer.py tests/test_skill_contracts.py tests/test_monitor_invocation_docs.py tests/test_skills_name_no_host_path.py, each with first line `revision: <full sha>`, show zero added failures by id. The command is never run with --write against the real user settings.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.8,
    "goal": "`reckon hooks install --scope user` prints the coordinator hook settings fragment, merging it into the settings file only when --write is given.",
